            {
                "entry_id": "6fd43a7c-69bd-3268-aee5-6fc3db7cce9c",
                "word": "Scrabble",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                        "entry_id": "6fd43a7c-69bd-3268-aee5-6fc3db7cce9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jeu de lettres où les joueurs forment des mots en plaçant des lettres sur une grille."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f10a68b-709c-4680-8058-6eb530559d6e",
                                "sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                                "text": "– Je me défends plus qu’honnêtement au scrabble mais cela n’a rien à voir, c’est de la stratégie, tandis que vous… Vous vous êtes entraîné ? Vous vous êtes exercé en collectionnant les pages « Enrichissez votre vocabulaire » de Sélection du Reader’s digest ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "facd5c81-40d4-4d40-aa20-481b01a6f483",
                                "sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                                "text": "De toutes façons, elle était vieille\nEt puis elle me battait au Scrabble\nElle avait une tête de sharpeï\nEt ses cadeaux étaient minables"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e2fd4c9-fcda-4873-be18-e2c33513249f",
                                "sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                                "text": "Malgré ce succès « so french », le top des jeux les plus vendus reste marqué par les mêmes titres depuis des décennies : Monopoly, Scrabble, Cluedo, Uno…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7d7754f-1358-4a27-97d6-8bc6d584a291",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fd43a7c-69bd-3268-aee5-6fc3db7cce9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                        "target_lang_word": "Scrabble",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Scrabble",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ba1b309-c009-3438-abc8-35b453399a11",
                                        "entry_id": "7332932d-d513-36ba-a77b-ad72dcb01cab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Brettspiel für zwei bis vier Spieler, das mit dem Ziel, aus Buchstabensteinen Wörter zu legen und damit Punkte zu erzielen, gespielt wird"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f0da12d-ce4c-4593-9208-eb9c88703ea6",
                                                "sense_id": "8ba1b309-c009-3438-abc8-35b453399a11",
                                                "text": "Das Grundprinzip des Scrabbles ist das des Kreuzworträtsels kombiniert mit Feldern, die zur Erhöhung der Buchstaben- und Wortwerte genutzt werden können."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bcd00bd2-d211-4cce-849d-25004f178d2c",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fd43a7c-69bd-3268-aee5-6fc3db7cce9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "679c3c35-a89d-393d-af88-fdb270ea70ec",
                        "target_lang_word": "Scrabble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Scrabble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "334693ef-85c5-3106-8d5e-7f38c2207491",
                                        "entry_id": "a8728737-1ccb-34a7-a274-f216985007ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A board game in which players draw letter tiles and take turns to make interlocking words like a crossword, scoring points according to the letters played and their positions on the board."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c9eb19a-100a-4b0b-a8ed-146c21cf6d59",
                                                "sense_id": "334693ef-85c5-3106-8d5e-7f38c2207491",
                                                "text": "So that's what's in the forbidden room! Scrabble! I want to laugh, shriek with laughter, fall off my chair. This was once the game of old women, old men, in the summers or in retirement villas, to be played when there was nothing good on television. Or of adolescents, once, long long ago. […] Now of course it's something different. Now it's forbidden, for us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78131cc9-ab72-415e-b969-fbf4e2ff21e4",
                                                "sense_id": "334693ef-85c5-3106-8d5e-7f38c2207491",
                                                "text": "Start by asking students if they ever watch Wheel of Fortune, or play games like Hangman or Scrabble.® Ask whether they have ever noticed any patterns in the frequency with which letters appear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58647ca9-1844-4534-b378-1281851c7d57",
                                                "sense_id": "334693ef-85c5-3106-8d5e-7f38c2207491",
                                                "text": "At the tournament level I dabble / But my tiles show a meaningless babble / I filled up my ranks / With a few extra blanks / And got busted for cheating at Scrabble"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
